@prefix ex: <http://example.org/kg#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# Nodes
ex:paper_0 a ex:Paper ; rdfs:label "A case of humidifier lung with a difficult differential diagnosis from COVID-19. This case report describes a 71-year-old man presenting with cough and dyspnea, initially suspected of having COVID-19 due to diffuse ground-glass opacities (GGOs) on a chest CT scan.  However, his symptoms rapidly improved, prompting further investigation. The patient's history revealed recent use of an ultrasonic hu…" .
ex:paper_1 a ex:Paper ; rdfs:label "Effect of Residents' Previous Laparoscopic Surgery Experience on Initial Robotic Suturing Experience. This study investigated the impact of gynecology residents' prior laparoscopic experience on their robotic suturing skills and the value of structured dry-lab training. Thirteen gynecology residents with no prior robotic surgery experience were divided into two groups based on their laparoscopic e…" .
ex:paper_2 a ex:Paper ; rdfs:label "Matrix metalloproteinase-9 inhibition or deletion attenuates portal hypertension in rodents. This study investigated the effects of matrix metalloproteinase-9 (MMP-9) inhibition or deletion on portal hypertension in rodent models. The research was motivated by the role of MMPs in extracellular matrix remodeling and angiogenesis, which are implicated in the development of portal hypertension. The s…" .
ex:field_0 a ex:Field ; rdfs:label "Medicine" .
ex:claim_0 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "Patients presenting with diffuse GGOs on chest CT scans should be evaluated for humidifier lung, especially if they have a history of humidifier use." .
ex:claim_1 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "HRCT findings, specifically ill-defined centrilobular nodules and mosaic attenuation, are helpful in differentiating humidifier lung from COVID-19." .
ex:claim_2 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "An inhalation challenge test (ICT) can be used to confirm the diagnosis of humidifier lung." .
ex:claim_3 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "The use of humidifiers may be associated with an increased risk of humidifier lung, especially during the COVID-19 pandemic." .
ex:claim_4 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "Residents with more laparoscopic experience (Group 2) showed a trend towards faster robotic suturing times compared to those with less experience (Group 1)." .
ex:claim_5 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "Residents with less laparoscopic experience (Group 1) had significantly lower mean suture times for laparoscopic suturing compared to those with more experience (Group 2)." .
ex:claim_6 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "The study supports the importance of structured dry-lab training in the initial phase of teaching both laparoscopic and robotic suturing skills." .
ex:claim_7 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "For all residents, the average time for laparoscopic suturing was 382 ± 159 seconds, while robotic suturing took 326 ± 196 seconds." .
ex:claim_8 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "MMP-9 inhibition with minocycline reduces portal pressure in BDL rats." .
ex:claim_9 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "MMP-9 inhibition with minocycline reduces superior mesenteric artery (SMA) flow in BDL rats." .
ex:claim_10 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "MMP-9 inhibition with minocycline decreases plasma VEGF concentration in BDL rats." .
ex:claim_11 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "MMP-9 inhibition with SB-3CT reduces portal pressure in BDL rats." .
ex:claim_12 a ex:Claim ; rdfs:label "MMP-9 gene deletion attenuates portal hypertension in BDL mice." .
ex:method_0 a ex:Method ; rdfs:label "This study is a case report detailing the diagnosis and management of a 71-year-old Japanese man presenting with cough and dyspnea. The patient's history included a 1-week history of cough and dyspnea. He had a 36 pack-year history of cigarette smoking.  The patient denied any pets or recent sick contacts. The patient presented with tachypnea (26 breaths/min) and hypoxemia (SpO2, 93% on room air),…" .
ex:method_1 a ex:Method ; rdfs:label "The study was approved by the Institutional Review Board at the University of Texas Medical Branch. Thirteen gynecology residents participated: four PGY3s and nine PGY4s. None had prior robotic surgery experience. All residents received a didactic lecture on MIS suturing. Group 1 included all PGY3s and two MIS-naive PGY4s. Group 2 comprised the more MIS-experienced PGY4s (≥3 previous MIS experienc…" .
ex:method_2 a ex:Method ; rdfs:label "The study employed a combination of in vivo experiments using rodent models of liver cirrhosis. Male Sprague-Dawley rats (240-270 g) and male MMP-9 KO mice (C57BL/6 background) and their WT littermates were used. Biliary cirrhosis was induced in rats and mice via BDL. Rats were randomly assigned to receive minocycline (120 mg/kg/day, oral gavage), SB-3CT (0.16 mg/kg/day, i.p.), or vehicle for four…" .
ex:result_0 a ex:Result ; rdfs:label "The patient presented with cough and dyspnea. Initial chest X-ray and CT scans showed diffuse GGOs. SARS-CoV-2 antigen and PCR tests were negative. The patient's symptoms improved rapidly with initial treatment. HRCT revealed ill-defined centrilobular nodules and mosaic attenuation.  An ICT resulted in cough, dyspnea, fever (37.5°C), and hypoxemia, with an increased alveolar-arterial oxygen tensio…" .
ex:result_1 a ex:Result ; rdfs:label "The mean suturing times were compared between PGY3 and PGY4 residents. For all residents, the average time for laparoscopic suturing was 382 ± 159 seconds, and for robotic suturing, it was 326 ± 196 seconds (P = 0.12). PGY3s had a shorter suturing time than PGY4s in both robotic and laparoscopic suturing. The PGY4 group showed a statistically significant difference (P = 0.02) between robotic (337…" .
ex:result_2 a ex:Result ; rdfs:label "Minocycline significantly reduced PP in BDL rats (p = 0.008), decreased SMA flow (p = 0.023) and CI (p = 0.002). Minocycline also significantly decreased plasma VEGF concentration (BDL-V vs. BDL-M: 16.71 ± 0.96 vs. 13.81 ± 0.73 ρg/ml, p = 0.028) and downregulated mesenteric protein expressions of MMP-9 (0.8043 ± 0.1676 vs. 0.3838 ± 0.0761, p = 0.033), iNOS (0.7789 ± 0.0806 vs. 0.5378 ± 0.0616, p =…" .
ex:evidence_0 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "The patient presented with diffuse GGOs on chest CT, and the diagnosis of humidifier lung was confirmed after a detailed history of humidifier use and HRCT interpretation." .
ex:evidence_1 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "The HRCT scan revealed ill-defined centrilobular nodules and mosaic attenuation, which are typical of HP but atypical of COVID-19, supporting the diagnosis of humidifier lung." .
ex:evidence_2 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "The ICT with the humidifier induced symptoms and physiological changes in the patient, confirming the diagnosis of humidifier lung." .
ex:evidence_3 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "The patient's humidifier use, combined with the increasing use of humidifiers during the COVID-19 pandemic, suggests a potential association." .
ex:evidence_4 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "Residents in Group 2 had a lower mean suture time on the robot compared to Group 1, although this difference did not achieve statistical significance (P = 0.5)." .
ex:evidence_5 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "Residents in Group 1 had a significantly lower mean suture time than those in Group 2 for laparoscopic suturing (P = 0.009)." .
ex:evidence_6 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "The study found that PGY3s, who received dry-lab training, had shorter suturing times compared to PGY4s, who had more experience but did not receive additional dry-lab training." .
ex:evidence_7 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "The average time for laparoscopic suturing was 382 ± 159 seconds, and for robotic suturing, it was 326 ± 196 seconds (P = 0.12)." .
ex:evidence_8 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "Minocycline treatment significantly reduced portal pressure in BDL rats (p = 0.008) compared to vehicle." .
ex:evidence_9 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "Minocycline significantly decreased SMA flow in BDL rats (p = 0.023)." .
ex:evidence_10 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "Minocycline significantly decreased the plasma VEGF concentration (BDL-V vs. BDL-M: 16.71 ± 0.96 vs. 13.81 ± 0.73 ρg/ml, p = 0.028)." .
ex:evidence_11 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "SB-3CT reduced PP (p = 0.019) in BDL rats." .
ex:evidence_12 a ex:Evidence ; rdfs:label "MMP-9 KO BDL mice had significantly lower PP compared with WT BDL mice (12.1 ± 0.5 vs. 7.8 ± 0.7 mmHg, p = 0.007)." .
ex:implication_0 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "Clinicians should include humidifier lung in the differential diagnosis of patients with similar symptoms and radiological findings, particularly in the context of increased humidifier use." .
ex:implication_1 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "Radiologists and pulmonologists should carefully interpret HRCT findings in conjunction with clinical history to differentiate between humidifier lung and COVID-19." .
ex:implication_2 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "The ICT can be a valuable diagnostic tool for confirming humidifier lung when the diagnosis is uncertain." .
ex:implication_3 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "Clinicians should be aware of the potential for humidifier lung in patients using humidifiers, particularly during respiratory illness outbreaks." .
ex:implication_4 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "Prior laparoscopic experience may facilitate the learning of robotic suturing skills, but further research with a larger sample size is needed to confirm this relationship." .
ex:implication_5 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "This finding suggests that the skills acquired in laparoscopic surgery may not directly translate to improved performance in laparoscopic suturing, or that other factors contribute to the difference in performance." .
ex:implication_6 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "Structured training in a dry-lab setting is crucial for developing fundamental surgical skills, regardless of prior experience." .
ex:implication_7 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "Robotic suturing may be faster than laparoscopic suturing, but the difference was not statistically significant in this study, likely due to the small sample size." .
ex:implication_8 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "This supports the potential of MMP-9 inhibition as a therapeutic strategy for portal hypertension." .
ex:implication_9 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "This suggests that minocycline may improve portal hypertension by reducing portal blood inflow." .
ex:implication_10 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "This suggests that minocycline may reduce portal hypertension by reducing angiogenesis." .
ex:implication_11 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "This supports the potential of MMP-2 and MMP-9 inhibition as a therapeutic strategy for portal hypertension." .
ex:implication_12 a ex:Implication ; rdfs:label "This provides further evidence for the role of MMP-9 in the pathogenesis of portal hypertension." .

